        "original_id": "0ee09274-6c49-57b5-9be9-210df6632931",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Reno–Tahoe International Airport, Washoe County, Nevada, Reno, Lake Tahoe, Las Vegas, Fort Reno, Oklahoma\n- People: Jesse L. Reno\n- Organizations: United States Army\n- Roles: Union General\n- Events: Mexican–American War, Utah War, American Civil War, Battle of South Mountain\n- Topics: airport naming, airport identifiers, airport location and traffic\n\nFacts:\n- Jesse Lee Reno was born on April 20, 1823.\n- Jesse L. Reno was a career United States Army officer who served in the Mexican–American War, the Utah War, on the western frontier, and as a Union General during the American Civil War.\n- Jesse L. Reno died at the Battle of South Mountain on September 14, 1862, during the American Civil War.\n- Fort Reno in Oklahoma was named for General Jesse L. Reno.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport is named after Jesse L. Reno and Lake Tahoe.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport is a public and military use airport located three nautical miles southeast of downtown Reno in Washoe County, Nevada.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport has the identifiers IATA RNO, ICAO KRNO, and FAA LID RNO.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport is Nevada's second busiest commercial airport after McCarran International Airport in Las Vegas.",
